````markdown
# M153 — Execution and authoring review remediation

**Owner:** Ramen. **Parallel-safe:** no.
**Planning approval:** Owner-approved standalone reconciliation on 2026-10-29 (“Approve + create suggested.txt”), amended by “update M153 using your recommendation” for all four M153 planning-review recommendations. Planning only; no execution, commit or grant activation.
**State:** Complete; M153.1–M153.5 `[+]`; whole review 1/10 passed (no P1/P2); retired 2026-10-29. Goal run: COMMIT_POLICY none (owner choice 2026-10-29), no commits.
**Specification:** [milestone.md](milestone.md#m153).
**Dependencies:** Retired [M150](../docs/history/status-M150.md), [M151](../docs/history/status-M151.md), [M152](../docs/history/status-M152.md), all accepted; no active blocker.
**Authorization:** Requirements live in the specification; none activated here.

**Review provenance.** *`/code-review high since eade545`* (Claude Code review, 2026-10-29), findings F01–F10 in source order; source priority not supplied. Review baseline `eade5454a79b0ade5c1d949f83f645355b9a10c8`..HEAD; revalidated at `25343bfea14c24fbb74766c06ba3b20e0890da92` with a clean worktree. F06 accepted by the owner as intended M152 scope (no row). Intake is not a review iteration.

**Planning-review provenance.** *M153 planning review — 2026-10-29*, findings PR-F01–PR-F04 (qualified source F01–F04); source and local priorities P1/P2/P2/P2. Source baseline not supplied; revalidated at `25343bfea14c24fbb74766c06ba3b20e0890da92` including the existing uncommitted M153 specification, status and launch reference. All four are confirmed amendments to pending owners in the specification. The review's focused existing tests passed across `executor`, `executor/udon`, `run` and `internal/wflowservice`, using the documented retained cache for the local Udon pin; these are baseline checks, not acceptance of the planned fixes. Review counter remains 0.

## Tasks

| Item | State | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| M153.1 — Credential redaction precision | `[+]` | F01/F02 (local P2), PR-F01 (source/local P1). Evidence: `executor/sensitive.go` registers every string field/variant, ignores json.Number/int/bool and can overwrite colliding redacted keys; `executor/udon/adapter.go` requires a string apiKey. Separate explicitly non-secret metadata; protect unknown fields and every nonempty resolved secret, including short/scalar/encoded values and key echoes. Fail closed on key collisions. No length exemption. Prove non-secret precision and secret protection together. Lineage: M150. **Delivered:** `SensitiveValues.AddCredentials` skips only an explicit allowlist of non-secret configuration fields (`type`, `region`, scopes, token/auth/redirect URLs, expiry; names compared ignoring case, `_` and `-`) and registers every other field, including unknown, short and scalar values; `AddData` now registers json.Number, ints, bools, floats, string slices and normalized containers in string form. Colliding redacted map keys get distinct deterministic placeholders and their values are redacted, so no entry is lost and no key leaks. The data-file resolver registers the environment-resolved fields of the selected group, and an apiKey/bearer field may be a string, number or boolean; any other shape gets an accurate non-`MissingError` error (wrapping left to M153.4). Call sites: `executor/executor.go`, `run/run.go`. **Evidence:** new tests in `executor/sensitive_test.go` and `executor/udon/adapter_test.go` fail against the previous source (4 of 5 redaction tests, 3 of 3 adapter tests; `TestRedactedKeyEchoesStayRedacted` is a retained protection that already held) and pass after the change. `go test ./...` 42 packages ok in 5m52s, `go vet ./...`, `go test -race ./executor/... ./run` and the existing race gate (`internal/gui`, `internal/wflowservice`, `internal/apiservice`), `git diff --check` all pass, offline with the retained Udon `c7e360dd` module cache. **Environment note:** the first full and race attempts failed with `disk quota exceeded` writing link output to the `/tmp` tmpfs (not a test failure); the passing runs set `TMPDIR`/`GOTMPDIR` to a private 0700 directory beside the retained Go caches. Not covered: `make ui-*` (no `web/` change). |
| M153.2 — Run data merge and evidence durability | `[+]` | F03/F10 (local P2), PR-F03 (source/local P2). Evidence: `run/run.go:112-127` overwrites document inputs; `:244-269` uses caller ctx for status/response evidence, discards status/run-event errors and replaces execution errors with response-recording errors. Refuse input conflicts; use bounded cancellation-independent cleanup for status, detailed events and terminal response. Attempt terminal recording after status failure and retain both execution/recording errors after redaction. Test cancellation and injected write failures. Lineage: M150. **Delivered (uncommitted, `COMMIT_POLICY: none`):** `run.Execute` refuses `--data` inputs when the document declares `variables.inputs` (`run.data_invalid`, before approval and in check mode), matching the adapter. `executeTarget` records status, detailed run events and the terminal response on a `context.WithoutCancel` context bounded by `evidenceRecordTimeout` (30s); a recording failure no longer stops later records (the response is still attempted after a status failure) and is reported, redacted, alongside the execution error (`evidence recording failed: …`), with the result kept when the execution itself succeeded. A small `evidenceRecorder` interface lets tests inject failures. **Evidence:** new `run/run_evidence_test.go`; reverting each fix in turn makes its tests fail (conflict: 2 subtests; cancellation: fake-recorder and real-SQLite tests, `status_observation` missing; combined errors: 3 subtests) and restoring it passes. `go test ./run ./executor/... ./cmd/...`, `go vet`, `go test -race ./run ./executor/...` pass; full suite is deferred to milestone closure. |
| M153.3 — Request expressions and literal escapes | `[+]` | F04 (local P2): `executor/udon/adapter.go:432-442` rejects any array containing an expression wrapper. F09 (local P2): `internal/wflowservice/workflow_plan_lower.go:159-163` strips `$literal:` for non-fnct ops; `adapter.go:337,383` decodes literals only with the declared-function extension; `workflow_plan_data.go:156`. Lineage: M150/M151. **Delivered (uncommitted, `COMMIT_POLICY: none`):** F04: an array that holds references is now composed by the adapter into one runtime expression (`[variables.inputs.a, step.received_body, 3, true, null, […]]`), because the retained runtime evaluates `$expr` only as a whole attribute value and not inside a tuple; the array may hold only plain-traversal references, numbers, booleans, null and nested such arrays. **Limit recorded:** the runtime does not carry quoted text inside a wrapper intact, so text or objects next to a reference in one list are refused with an accurate message (was "unsupported array shape") instead of being composed; the same limit applies to any non-traversal wrapper source. F09: Lower keeps a `$literal:` marker for non-function operations only where unwrapping would read as a reference (contains `$variables.`/`$steps.` or starts with `$literal:`; also for `literal:`, `$const:`, `template:` prefixes) and marks that operation with the existing `x-ramen-declared-function-literals` extension, which the adapter, preflight and runbook already honor; plain literals and declared-function output are unchanged. `deriveDataJSON` skips `$literal:` values for every operation except legacy non-catalog function steps (existing behavior kept). Documented in `AUTHORING.md` A.4. **Evidence:** new tests in `executor/udon/adapter_test.go` (array composition, real-runtime evaluation through the `identity` function, refusal cases, literal escape for non-function operations) and `internal/wflowservice/workflow_plan_literal_test.go`; reverting each part (array composition, lowering escape, data derivation) makes its tests fail and restoring passes; one older test row that asserted arrays must be rejected was replaced by the new array tests. `go test ./internal/wflowservice ./internal/runbook ./internal/workflowplanops ./internal/workflowshape ./executor/... ./run ./tests` (tests 354s), `go vet` pass. Downstream: lowered output changes only for ambiguous literals (Kinet-fixture candidate already notes it). |
| M153.4 — Credential fallback and OAuth concurrency | `[+]` | F07/F08 (local P2), PR-F04 (source/local P2). Evidence: `executor/udon/adapter.go:712-745` returns inapplicable-scheme/OAuth-field errors unwrapped and holds `cacheMu` across token exchange; absent groups already return `MissingError`. Prove OR fallback from a present unusable group, retaining absent-group coverage separately, and prove genuine token-exchange failure stays fatal. Per-key single flight permits independent OAuth exchanges. Race check `./executor/...` required. Lineage: M150. **Delivered (uncommitted, `COMMIT_POLICY: none`):** every data-file resolver outcome that means "this group cannot satisfy this alternative" — an apiKey scheme without a declared field or whose field is absent, `openIdConnect`/unsupported scheme types, http basic, and OAuth2/bearer groups holding no token material (`AuthorizationRequiredError`) — now returns `credentials.MissingError`, so udon's OR security evaluation tries the next alternative. Genuine failures stay fatal: a wrong-shaped apiKey value, an incomplete OAuth2 group, an ambiguous binding match and a failed token exchange. OAuth token acquisition moved to a per-key single-flight cache (`oauthTokenCache`): the exchange no longer runs under the cache lock, so independent bindings exchange in parallel, concurrent callers of one key share one exchange, and a waiter retries with its own context when the shared exchange ended with only its caller's cancellation. **Evidence:** new `executor/udon/credential_fallback_test.go` (resolver table, genuine-failure table, loopback OpenAPI run with `security: [basic, key]` proving fallback from a present unusable group plus the absent-group and no-usable-alternative cases, and three concurrency tests). Reverting the `MissingError` wrapping fails 6 table rows and the loopback fallback case (the "unsupported authentication scheme" error); serializing the exchange under the lock fails the independent-exchange test after 5s; restoring passes. `go test -race ./executor/... ./run`, `go vet` pass. Tests use only loopback servers and synthetic values. |
| M153.5 — Local-function compatibility | `[+]` | F05 (local P2), PR-F02 (source/local P2). Evidence: `workflow_plan_functions.go:36` pins the digest; Lower calls the same validation; `web/src/useEditBoundMappings.ts:67` submits saved refs to the bind endpoint. Keep new binds strict; Lower reports compatible saved digest drift. Backend loads the same saved checked step, requires its exact reference and current compatibility of saved/proposed mappings, then validates and persists a refreshed digest. Reject new/altered stale refs and incompatible/non-catalog binds without writes. Test edit success and refusal paths; correct the comment. Lineage: M152. **Delivered (uncommitted, `COMMIT_POLICY: none`):** `internal/wflowservice/workflow_plan_functions.go` splits the check: `validateLocalFunctionBinding` stays strict for new binds (declared source, current digest, catalog fields); `validateSavedLocalFunction` (used by Lower) checks the function name and input/output fields only and returns digest drift; the misleading "remain readable" comment is replaced. `Lower` now accepts a compatible saved step with a stale digest and reports it in `LowerReport.LocalFunctionDrift`, surfaced as `local_function_drift` on the materialize response (backend only; no `web/` change, so UI gates not run and UI display of drift is not added). `BindWorkflowStep` keeps strict validation first; only when it fails on a stale `fnct` reference does it load the saved plan and call `refreshStaleLocalFunctionRef`, which refreshes to the current digest only if the saved step is `checked`, its saved reference equals the submitted one exactly, and both saved and proposed mappings pass the catalog shape check; otherwise the original strict error is returned and nothing is written. F06 behavior unchanged. **Evidence:** `workflow_plan_functions_test.go` replaces the old assertion that a stale digest must fail to lower with compatible-stale-lowers-with-drift, unknown-function/incompatible-fields-refused, materialize-surfaces-drift, edit-refreshes-digest and a 7-case refusal table that also asserts the saved plan bytes are unchanged; weakening each piece in turn (strict Lower, no refresh, unchecked refresh) fails the matching tests and restoring passes. `docs/m152-local-functions.md` updated. |

## Review

Review gate iterations: 1 — PASSED (2026-10-29). Base `25343bfea14c24fbb74766c06ba3b20e0890da92`; whole-milestone diff = commit `02b9b67` (M153.1) plus the uncommitted worktree (M153.2–M153.5) under `COMMIT_POLICY: none`. The review read the full diff for correctness, regressions, failure semantics, boundary drift, stale docs and missing tests, and checked acceptance fidelity row by row; it found no P1 or P2 issue and made no fix.

Verification: `GOWORK=off go vet ./...` clean; `go test ./... -count=1` 42 packages ok (tests 353s); `go test -race ./internal/gui ./internal/wflowservice ./internal/apiservice ./executor/... ./run` ok; `git diff --check` clean. Offline with the retained Udon `c7e360dd` module cache; `TMPDIR`/`GOTMPDIR` on disk because `/tmp` tmpfs hit `disk quota exceeded` during link steps. No `web/` change, so UI gates were not run.

Lower-severity carry-forward (no owner row; documented limits, not defects):
- An array that holds references cannot also hold quoted text or objects, because the retained runtime does not carry quoted text inside a wrapper intact; the adapter refuses it with an accurate message (previously any such array was refused). Candidate for a future Udon/runtime change.
- A wrong-shaped apiKey field (non-scalar) stays a fatal error rather than an OR fallback.
- `local_function_drift` is returned by the materialize API; the web UI does not display it yet.
